fact WorkItem(id: "WI-989", description: some(value: "SCALAND: `firstLocated` STILL FALLS BACK TO `Span.empty`, SO WI-964's \"NO PARSER-BUILT TERM IS SPANLESS\" IS FALSE ON SOURCE A USER CAN WRITE. `AnthillParser.firstLocated` degrades to `Span.empty` when it finds no located child, and `typeExprToRef` then mints name-bearing terms with no location — while `IR.scala`'s doc on `nameBearingWithoutSpan` asserts the set is \"EMPTY for every parser-built store\". MEASURED on the WI-976/WI-983 HEAD through that very probe: `rule e(?x) :- p(Foo[F = (?a) -> ?b])` yields 3 locationless name-bearing terms (`TypeExtractor.Arrow`, `TypeExtractor.EffectsRows`, `EffectExpression.empty_row`); `p(Foo[E = {}])` yields 1 (`effects_rows`); `rule a(?f) :- p(?f: (?a, ?b) -> ?c)` yields 11, including `Ref(_0)`, `NamedTupleElement` and `List.cons`/`nil`. Control: `p(Foo[F = (S) -> S])` yields 0. These are `Foo[...]` InstArg children, so they reach `Loader.reallocTerm`'s `Fn` arm and `resolveName(kb, name, scope, errors, Span.empty)` — a locationless load diagnostic, which is precisely the defect WI-957 exists to have closed. THE COVERAGE GAP IS THE INTERESTING HALF: `ParseSpanCoverageTest`'s grammar tour writes `S` at every type leaf, and `S` is exactly the passing control above, so that suite CANNOT catch this and did not. WORK: give the fallback a real span — the enclosing construct's is available at every call site — and delete `Span.empty` from the production path so the doc's claim is structural. Then extend the coverage fixture with `?var` type leaves, since a corpus of ground leaves measures nothing here. ACCEPTANCE: `nameBearingWithoutSpan` is empty for the three measured sources above, asserted as a test rather than as a doc sentence. Say at the site which test fails when the change is backed out. Found by code review (2026-08-04). Related: WI-964, WI-957, WI-961."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "scaland-sbt-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-08-04T21:34:44Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-989", name: "scaland")
